      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. 15-9260"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Tuesday, February 28, 2017"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You said nothing in 924(c), but there is a bar on concurrent sentencing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it's 20 years later, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stoler",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STOLER: Well, that -- I -- I submit, Your Honor, that -- that turns around the determination to be made. The independence -- the -- the separate crime, the separate punishment goes to 924(c). It has to happen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Well, I think it's true that Congress could have written it more clearly, but we think that Congress here, when you take a look at both the provisions of 924(c) and then read them in conjunction with the provisions of the Sentencing Reform Act makes sufficiently clear Congress's intent that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what we would have to argue in that case is that the Congress would have known that the traditional place that judges determine the aggregate length of a sentence, when there are multiple offenses carrying terms of imprisonment, is in the determination that -- of whether the sentences run concurrently or consecutively."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we're in this kind of weird -- we're -- we're in this weird world that this Court has created where the guidelines are advisory, but then they're not advisory, and so that's why we have this problem; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stoler",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's no affirmative ban in district courts considering 924(c) sentencing when considering the predicate offenses, and given the overarching theme of -- of discretion and parsimony pervades."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-9260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:02 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
